{
    "file": "Consultative_and_Digital_Selling.docx",
    "title": "Consultative and Digital Selling",
    "duration": "3 Days",
    "overview": [
        "Modern selling combines consultative conversations with informed use of digital channels and sales technology. Customers research alternatives independently, interact across multiple touchpoints, and expect sellers to understand their business needs before recommending a solution. Effective sales professionals must diagnose customer challenges, build trust, communicate value, and use digital tools without losing the personal quality of the relationship.",
        "This three-day course develops a practical approach to consultative and digital selling, from prospect research and discovery to solution alignment, digital engagement, opportunity management, objection handling, and customer follow-up. Participants learn how to integrate virtual meetings, professional social platforms, CRM systems, digital content, and data-informed outreach into a coherent sales process.",
        "The course uses applied sales cases, discovery simulations, digital prospecting exercises, value-proposition development, virtual selling practice, and opportunity-planning workshops to strengthen customer conversations and improve sales execution."
    ],
    "audience": [
        "Sales executives, account managers, business-development professionals, inside sales teams, field sales representatives, relationship managers, sales supervisors, customer-facing consultants, and professionals responsible for generating and developing sales opportunities through face-to-face and digital channels."
    ],
    "methodology": [
        "Interactive presentations, facilitated discussions, customer-needs analysis, consultative questioning exercises, prospecting and outreach workshops, social-selling cases, virtual-meeting simulations, CRM and pipeline scenarios, objection-handling role plays, peer feedback, and individual sales action planning."
    ],
    "competencies": [
        "Consultative selling and customer discovery",
        "Digital prospecting and professional social selling",
        "Customer and account research",
        "Value-based solution positioning",
        "Active listening and questioning",
        "Virtual sales communication",
        "CRM and opportunity management",
        "Digital content and outreach planning",
        "Objection handling and negotiation",
        "Sales follow-up and relationship development"
    ],
    "objectivesIntro": [
        "By the end of the course, participants will be able to:"
    ],
    "objectives": [
        "Explain how consultative selling differs from transactional selling and how digital channels affect the buying journey.",
        "Research prospective customers and identify relevant business priorities, stakeholders, and buying signals.",
        "Plan and conduct discovery conversations that reveal needs, constraints, and desired outcomes.",
        "Use questioning, listening, and summarizing to build trust and validate customer requirements.",
        "Develop solution recommendations and value propositions linked to customer outcomes.",
        "Use professional digital channels to initiate and sustain relevant sales conversations.",
        "Conduct effective virtual sales meetings and demonstrations.",
        "Apply CRM practices to manage contact information, opportunities, activities, and next steps.",
        "Respond constructively to objections and commercial concerns.",
        "Develop a coordinated consultative and digital selling plan for a realistic opportunity."
    ],
